# Commit after each change

After you finish a distinct change (feature, fix, or requested edit), create a git commit before stopping or starting the next change.

- Do not wait to be asked. Treat each finished change as a commit request.
- One commit per change. Do not batch unrelated work into a single commit.
- Follow this repository's existing commit message style.
- Never update git config, skip hooks, force-push, or amend unless the user explicitly asks.
- Do not commit secrets such as `.env` or credential files.

```text
# ❌ BAD
Finish a joystick change and a minimap change, then make one combined commit.

# ✅ GOOD
Commit the joystick change as soon as it works, then commit the minimap change separately.
```
